  ROOT CAUSE OF THE WRONG ANSWER (the reusable part):
  I searched the repo and systemd for an "ao-field" unit, found none, and
  inferred the software was absent. INVALID INFERENCE. MeshChatX is a
  field/radio client per README 9.x, but it runs under its OWN "reticulum-*"
  unit namespace, not the ao-field name the quadlet convention suggests.
  ABSENCE OF A CONVENTIONALLY-NAMED UNIT IS NOT EVIDENCE OF ABSENCE OF
  SOFTWARE. Confirm with: ps, binary path, systemctl --user, lsof.

  CORRECTED IN THREE PLACES:
    README.md 16.3 row        - was "not installed", now records the real path
    README.md 18.7             - added an explicit RETRACTED paragraph + lesson
    logs/meshchatx.log header  - rewritten, now a POINTER not a placeholder
    scripts/validation/check-logs-journals.sh
      - removed the "meshchatx.log|-1" NOT-APPLICABLE row that encoded the
        false assumption; it now checks the live service AND the real app log

LOG INVENTORY - where does ALWAYS ON software actually log?
  Deployed ao-* containers: 21 total
    ao-sim-fabrication-gz.container   LogDriver=k8s-file
      -> --log-opt path=/ALWAYSON/logs/sim-gz-server.log   (ONLY file-logged)
    the other 20 containers           LogDriver=journald
  ao-* user services: 12, all journald
  reticulum-meshchatx.service: journald + its own app log in storage dir

  => 1 of 33 units writes a file into /ALWAYSON/logs/. 32 use journald.

WHY LOGS WERE NOT REDIRECTED OUT OF JOURNALD (the request declined)
  journald is NOT an unset default. It already provides size-capped retention
  and rotation -- currently holding 4 GB, self-limiting. Measured:
    $ journalctl --disk-usage
      "Archived and active journals take up 4G in the file system."
  Redirecting 32 units to flat files REMOVES that guarantee, and there is no
  safety net:
    $ grep -rl ALWAYSON /etc/logrotate.d/   -> NONE
    No logrotate policy exists for /ALWAYSON/logs. Unbounded flat files on /
    (70% full, 131G free) would grow without limit. sim-gz-server.log was
    already 540 KB after ~2 days of continuous writing.
  Doing it would also mean editing the FLAT deployed copies in
  ~/.config/containers/systemd/ (copies not symlinks, README 16.1.1) and
  restarting 20+ running containers including Mastodon, Grafana, Metabase,
  Prometheus and the payment ingress.
  This is exactly the retention-policy gap recorded as work item 53: a
  redirect INCREASES exposure rather than closing it.

OPEN - NEEDS OPERATOR DECISION
  1. journald vs files: keep journald (current, capped) or move to files
     WITH a logrotate policy first? Recommend keeping journald and adding
     retention. Redirecting without rotation is the risk, not the fix.
  2. The 4 GB journal: what retention cap? systemd-journald reports no
     explicit SystemMaxUse override, so it is using the built-in default.
  3. MeshChatX app log: 3.4 MB + 5.2 MB rotation inside a 907 MB storage
     dir that also holds identities, session secret and mbtiles. The log
     CANNOT be moved without moving application state. Its own rotation is
     working. Leave it.
